('1dac6b99-82c0-4c9a-84a5-cf032de45ceb', 'f29ac8eceb324750ab7ce4b017128852', 'assistant', 'Sure, I can help you create a simple photo card. Here\'s an example of what the JSON code might look like:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"format\": \"generic-banner\",\n  \"title\": \"Photocard Design Example\",\n  \"layers\": [\n    {\n      \"type\": \"image\",\n      \"name\": \"Photo Card Background\",\n      \"imageUrl\": \"https://example.com/photo_card_background.jpg\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"type\": \"text\",\n      \"name\": \"Text on the Photo Card\",\n      \"content\": \"This is a photo card design example.\",\n      \"x\": 10,\n      \"y\": 50\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\nReplace `\"https://example.com/photo_card_background.jpg\"` with your actual image URL. This will create a simple, generic-style photo card.\n\nIf you need more customization or specific elements added to the design (like text styles, shapes, etc.), let me know!', '2026-10-21 15:33:23', 'qwen2.5:1.5b', 3536, 196, 3732, NULL, NULL, 1),
('1dcc580c-1687-4e5c-935e-e0eb4abc94ff', '6c47fa1a2a39a9d9e3f9702d2d54d54e', 'assistant', 'The current Prime Minister of the United Kingdom as of July 2026 is Andy Burnham. He took office on 20 July 2026, succeeding Keir Starmer and becoming the first Prime Minister to belong to the Labour and Co-operative Party since Tony Blair in 1997.\n\nAndy Burnham was elected Member of Parliament for Leigh in June 2001. Prior to his tenure as Prime Minister, he served between 2007 and 2010 as Chief Secretary to the Treasury under Gordon Brown\'s government.\n\nIt is worth noting that Andy Burnham became Prime Minister on July 20, 2026, making him the longest-serving prime minister since Walpole in 18th century Britain.\n\n---\n**🌐 Verified with Google Search:**\n- [en.wikipedia.org](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Premiership_of_Andy_Burnham)\n- [gov.uk](https://www.gov.uk/government/people/andy-burnham)\n- [gov.uk](https://www.gov.uk/government/ministers/prime-minister)\n- [en.wikipedia.org](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Prime_Minister_of_the_United_Kingdom)', '2026-10-21 00:09:54', 'nobrain1.0:latest', 640, 159, 799, NULL, NULL, 1),
('1dd36416-93d1-4456-857c-2e21d40c4255', '9cd06778a6cacccc5499d929db7b8d4c', 'assistant', '<think>\nThe user asks \"Hello, what model are you?\" They likely want to know about the model. The system says we are noBrain, an AI platform powered by AWS Bedrock (gpt-oss-120b). So we should answer in appropriate language (the user wrote in English). We should respond politely, mention that we are an AI based on GPT-OSS-120B, using AWS Bedrock, and maybe mention capabilities. Use markdown.\n</think>\n\n**Hello!** 👋  \n\nI’m **noBrain**, an AI conversational platform built on **AWS Bedrock** using the **gpt‑oss‑120b** model (a 120‑billion‑parameter open‑source version of GPT).  \n\n- **What this means:** I’m a large language model that can understand and generate text in multiple languages (including Bengali, Banglish, and English), answer questions, help with writing, coding, tutoring, brainstorming, and much more.  \n- **How I work:** Your prompts are processed by the gpt‑oss‑120b model hosted on AWS Bedrock, and I generate responses in real‑time.  \n\nFeel free to ask anything—you’ll get a helpful, fluent reply! 😊', '2026-10-28 19:50:04', 'openai.gpt-oss-120b-1:0', 138, 255, 393, NULL, NULL, 1),
